# Push every commit, then verify the deploy

This project is served from GitHub Pages at https://swirle13.github.io/batomon-calculator/,
built by `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` on push to `main`. The user validates changes against
that live site, so **a commit that is not pushed and deployed does not exist from their side**.

## Required

After any commit, push it:

```bash
git push origin main
```

Do not batch several commits and push later, and do not end a turn with unpushed work.

## Verify, don't assume

Pushing is not shipping. The deploy takes ~1 minute and the Pages workflow uses a
`concurrency: group: pages`, so a rapid second push can supersede an in-flight run.

```bash
gh run list --limit 3   # confirm completed/success for the SHA just pushed
```

For a user-visible change, confirm the live site serves the new bundle rather than trusting
the green check. The asset filenames are content-hashed, so comparing them against the local
build is a direct check that the deployed code is the code you wrote:

```bash
ls dist/assets/                                              # local hashes
curl -s https://swirle13.github.io/batomon-calculator/ | rg -o 'assets/index-[^"]*'
```

Matching hashes means the live site is running your build. Differing hashes mean the deploy
has not landed yet — say so rather than telling the user to reload.

## When a change "doesn't show up"

Check in this order before touching the code: is the commit pushed, did the run succeed, do
the deployed asset hashes match the local build, and is the user on the live site or on the
dev server (which Vite may have moved off port 5173 if it was occupied).
